  "requires_runtime": {
    "node": ">=22",
    "notes": "Skills and prompts need no runtime. The six document converters (docx-to-md, html-to-md, md-to-eml, md-to-html, md-to-txt, md-to-word) shell out through scripts/shared/tool-runner.cjs and additionally require pandoc on PATH; md-to-html and md-to-word require mermaid-cli on PATH only when the source contains Mermaid blocks. jszip is an optional faster path for md-to-word. Converter scripts resolve the shared runtime by relative depth (../../../scripts/shared), which is why scripts/shared/ sits at the payload root."
  },
  "upstream": {
    "notes": "Source-of-truth is the upstream repo. Mall vendors a specific tag; when upstream tags a new release, Mall automation flags the mismatch. Core is the plugin-native successor to Alex_ACT_Edition v4.2.0.",
    "repo": "https://github.com/fabioc-aloha/Alex_ACT_Core",
    "license": "MIT",
    "ref": "v0.6.6"
  },
  "instruction_scope": {
    "shipped": false,
    "reason": "Core authors 18 ACT instructions (17 always-on + 1 pattern-applied), but plugin.json has no instructions component field, so a plugin install cannot load them natively. install-constellation Step 6 separately copies the seventeen always-on resources from skills/install-constellation/bootstrap/ to ~/.copilot/instructions/ under an alex-act- prefix, consent-gated and receipt-backed. v0.6.2 adds deterministic repository workspace bootstrap, exact marketplace-version resolution, all-command installed-file fallback, bootstrap-only repair, and four-plane activation reporting. The complete payload retains config and scripts/shared at the 100-file Windows limit. Verified against Copilot CLI 1.0.77 and VS Code Chat 1.131."
  },
